## Tools

`tools/lldpmed_phone.py` is used for the endpoint side **as it stands**, as the dispatch
directs (STANDING-ORDERS §7: use the tool that exists). It emulates an LLDP-MED **Endpoint
Class III** IP phone — chassis and port ID = its MAC, system name `ck-phone`, system
capabilities Telephone, an LLDP-MED Capabilities TLV declaring Class III, and an inventory
hardware revision `CK-PHONE-EMU` — sends one LLDPDU a second, decodes every LLDPDU the switch
sends back, and writes everything it hears to a pcap. Run with `--no-dhcp`, because this bench
has no DHCP server in a voice VLAN and the DHCP phase is not what this case is about.

| tool | invocation |
| --- | --- |
| `tools/lldpmed_phone.py` | `tools/tb sudotool tb277 lldp1159 lldpmed_phone eth3 /tmp/lldp1159/<f>.pcap [--mac 00:00:5e:00:53:NN] --lldp-secs N --no-dhcp` |
| `tools/lldpwire.py` (new in T44296) | `tools/tb tool tb277 lldp1159 lldpwire /tmp/lldp1159/<f>.pcap --src e2:1a:ea:d4:70:43 --tlv` |
| `tools/lldpsend.py` (new in T44296) | `tools/tb sudotool tb277 lldp1159 lldpsend eth3 --count 2 --ttl 120 --chassis-mac ... --port-id ckPLAIN --caps station` — the **non-MED control neighbour** |
| `tools/tb capture` | `capture tb277 lldp1159 eth3 <secs> <out>.pcap ether proto 0x88cc` |
| `tools/tb cfg` / `ckcon` / `qmark` / `ping` / `ckreload` / `probe` | as in T44296 |

**`lldpmed_phone.py` status before this case:** *"generalised 2026-10-02, not re-verified on
hardware."* This run is its first hardware verification; its README status is updated with the
result.

