# STEP 4 — The DUT classifies the endpoint as LLDP-MED Endpoint Class III, with a non-MED control

**Why this step.** The other half of STEP 3: the DUT must not only advertise to the endpoint,
it must recognise what the endpoint is.

**The DUT's neighbour table:**
```
awplus#show lldp neighbors
Total number of neighbors on these ports .... 5

Local    Neighbor        Neighbor        Neighbor                System   MED
Port     Chassis ID      Port ID         Sys Name                Cap.     Ty Pwr
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1.0.2    0000.cd42.3029  port1.0.2
1.0.4    889d.98df.2602  port1.0.4
1.0.10   0000.5e00.5310  0000.5e00.5310  ck-phone                -----T-- 3
1.0.14   889d.98df.2602  port1.0.14
1.0.16   0000.cd42.3029  port1.0.16
```
`-----T--` is **Telephone** in the capability codes the command prints, and `MED Ty = 3` is
**Class III**.

**In detail** (`show lldp neighbors detail interface port1.0.10`, abridged):
```
  Chassis ID Type .................. MAC address
  Chassis ID ....................... 0000.5e00.5310
  Port ID Type ..................... MAC address
  System Name ...................... ck-phone
  System Capabilities - Supported .. Telephone
                      - Enabled .... Telephone
  LLDP-MED Device Type ............. Endpoint Class III
  LLDP-MED Capabilities ............ LLDP-MED Capabilities, Network Policy,
                                     Extended Power - PD, Inventory
  Inventory Management:
       Hardware Revision ........... CK-PHONE-EMU
```
Every field is what `lldpmed_phone.py` advertises, including the inventory string
`CK-PHONE-EMU`, and the DUT reads the endpoint's capability as **Extended Power - PD** (a
powered device) where its own is `[not supported]` (no PoE on the -56).

**The control — a non-MED neighbour on the SAME port at the SAME time.** A plain LLDPDU was
sent with `lldpsend.py`, advertising Station-only capability and no MED TLV at all:
```
awplus#show lldp neighbors interface port1.0.10
Total number of neighbors on these ports .... 2
1.0.10   0000.5e00.5310  0000.5e00.5310  ck-phone                -----T-- 3
1.0.10   0200.0000.00f0  ckPLAIN         ckplain                 -------S
```
**One port, one instant, two neighbours, two classifications.** The MED phone reads
`-----T--` with `MED Ty 3`; the plain neighbour reads `-------S` (Station only) with the **MED
columns blank**. The DUT classifies by what the frame advertises, not by the port it arrived
on — which is the claim, and it could not be made from the MED entry alone.

**STEP 4 verdict: PASS.**

