## Teardown and bench verification

**Teardown sent** — including the three lines the DUT had added or kept on its own:
```
awplus(config)#interface port1.0.10
awplus(config-if)#no switchport voice vlan
awplus(config-if)#no switchport voice vlan priority
awplus(config-if)#no switchport voice dscp
awplus(config-if)#no spanning-tree portfast         <- the implicit line from STEP 2
awplus(config)#vlan database
awplus(config-vlan)#no vlan 70
awplus#write
Building configuration...
[OK]
```
No `% ` line on any of them.

**Result:**
```
awplus#show running-config interface port1.0.10
interface port1.0.10
 switchport
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 10
```
— exactly the three lines it had before this case. `show vlan brief` no longer lists VLAN 70,
and `show startup-config` contains **no** `voice`, `vlan 70`, `ckVOICE` or `portfast` line;
its only LLDP line is `lldp run`.

**Running-config diff — twice, and both are empty.**
```
diff <pre-case running-config> <post-case running-config>   ->  RUNNING-CONFIG IDENTICAL
diff <T44296 pre-case running-config> <post-case>           ->  IDENTICAL TO GROUP-C STARTING STATE
```
Both 112 lines, byte for byte. **The DUT is exactly as group C found it at 14:52 NZDT**, after
two cases, two reloads and four `write`s.

(`tools/rcdiff.py` was run first and reported a single spurious line, `-15:48:01` — it keys on
`HH:MM:SS >>>` headers and mistook the next command's timestamp for config. The direct diff of
the extracted `show running-config` bodies above is the authoritative check, and it is clean.
Worth a note in the tool's entry, not a defect that affected this case.)

**Host legs re-ARPed after the reboot** (the same post-reload effect T44296 recorded):
`tools/tb ping tb277 eth3 10.38.22.34 3` and `... eth4 10.38.22.66 3` both **3 received, 0%
packet loss**.

**Closing probe**, against the swi_d-only template (u3 and u5 are locked out and must not be
touched — see "What could not be produced"):
```
tools/tb probe tb277 --consoles u2 --no-prompt --read-only --pdu 10.36.230.212 \
     --outlet u2=1 --name u2=swi_d --template /tmp/lldp1159/tb277-u2.setup \
     --out /tmp/lldp1159/bench-state-close3.md
MATCH -- the bench equals the template.
```
**Exit 0 MATCH.** The repo's `bench-setup/tb277/bench-state.md` was not overwritten; the probe
wrote to `/tmp`.

**Final wire check** (`m20_final.pcap`, 70 s): the DUT is back to **4 TLVs**, no MED TLV of any
kind, TTL 120 — the STEP 1 baseline, reached again from the other end of the case.

**Nothing left running on the box.** Every capture was a bounded `timeout <secs> tcpdump` that
printed its own `N packets captured` summary at exit; `lldpmed_phone.py` and `lldpsend.py` both
send a fixed number of frames and return. No watcher, no background sender, no framework run.

**Consoles.** u2 returned to `awplus login:`. **u3 and u5 were never opened by this case.**

